.Dd October 26, 2026
.Dt SSG 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssg
.Nd content directory format for ssg(1)
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A content directory holds a
.Pa site.toml ,
an HTML skeleton, an optional templates directory, markdown pages and any other files.
.Xr ssg 1
turns each page into
.Pa .html ,
.Pa .md
and
.Pa .txt
files in the dist directory and copies everything else.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
site/
  site.toml          configuration
  skeleton.html      HTML around every page
  templates/         for {{extend}} and {{include}}
    base.md
    partials/back.md
  .assetignore       files not to publish
  index.md           -> /
  about.md           -> /about/
  guide/index.md     -> /guide/
  guide/setup.md     -> /guide/setup/
  style.css          copied as is
.Ed
.Sh SITE.TOML
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dist = "dist"                  # required
templates = "templates"        # required
skeleton = "skeleton.html"     # required
base_url = "https://example.com"
clean = true
nested_repos = false
ignore = ["*.psd", "drafts/"]

[markdown]
html = true
scripts = false
heading_ids = true
autolinks = true
extensions = true
text_width = 80
.Ed
.Pp
Relative paths are relative to the content directory.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic dist No (string, required)
Output directory.
It must not be the content directory or contain it, must not contain the templates
directory or the skeleton, and none of its path components below the part it shares with
the content directory may start with
.Sq \&. .
It may be outside the content directory.
.It Ic templates No (string, required)
Templates directory.
It may be missing until a page uses
.Li {{extend}}
or
.Li {{include}} .
Nothing in it is published.
.It Ic skeleton No (string, required)
The HTML skeleton; see
.Sx SKELETON .
Not published.
.It Ic base_url No (string)
Site origin, such as
.Li https://example.com .
Trailing slashes are removed.
When set,
.Pa sitemap.xml
is written; see
.Sx SITEMAP .
.It Ic clean No (boolean, default true)
Empty dist before building, but only if
.Xr ssg 1
owns it: it holds the
.Pa .ssg-dist
marker, which a build writes into a dist that is missing, empty or already marked.
A non-empty dist without the marker is built over with a warning.
.It Ic nested_repos No (boolean, default false)
Also build subdirectories that contain a
.Pa .git
file or directory.
By default they are skipped with a note, so a tool checked out inside the site (for
example by CI) is not published.
.It Ic ignore No (array of strings)
Patterns in
.Pa .assetignore
syntax, relative to the content directory.
They come before every
.Pa .assetignore
rule, so those can override them.
.El
.Pp
The
.Ic [markdown]
table:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic html No (boolean, default true)
Pass raw HTML through.
False escapes it, so it shows as text.
.It Ic scripts No (boolean, default false)
With
.Ic html
on, let
.Li <script> ,
.Li <iframe> ,
.Li <object> ,
.Li <embed> ,
.Li <style>
and similar elements,
.Li on*
attributes and
.Li javascript: ,
.Li vbscript: ,
.Li file:
and non-image
.Li data:
URLs through.
False escapes those elements, drops those attributes and any raw HTML attribute holding such
a URL, and turns such URLs in markdown links and images into
.Li href="#"
or
.Li src="" .
HTML comments are removed.
.It Ic heading_ids No (boolean, default true)
Give every heading a GitHub-style id, deduplicated with
.Li -1 ,
.Li -2 ,
\&...
suffixes, unless it sets one with
.Li {#id} .
.It Ic autolinks No (boolean, default true)
GFM bare links:
.Li www.example.com ,
.Li https://example.com ,
.Li user@example.com .
Needs
.Ic extensions .
.It Ic extensions No (boolean, default true)
Everything beyond CommonMark; see
.Sx MARKDOWN .
False gives strict CommonMark syntax.
.It Ic text_width No (integer 0 to 100000, default 80)
Wrap column of the
.Pa .txt
output.
0 disables wrapping.
.El
.Pp
Unknown keys and tables are warnings, not errors.
A key's type must match: a string where a boolean is expected is an error.
.Ss TOML subset
Supported:
.Li #
comments, blank lines,
.Li [table]
headers, bare keys
.Pq Li A-Za-z0-9_-
and quoted keys,
.Li \(dqbasic\(dq
strings with the escapes
.Li \e\(dq \e\e \en \et \er \eb \ef \euXXXX \eUXXXXXXXX ,
.Li \(aqliteral\(aq
strings,
.Li true ,
.Li false ,
integers (optional sign,
.Sq _
separators), and arrays of strings, which may span lines and end with a comma.
A leading UTF-8 BOM and CRLF line endings are accepted.
.Pp
Not supported, each an error: dotted keys, floats, dates, inline tables, arrays of tables,
multi-line strings, arrays of anything but strings.
Duplicate keys and tables are errors.
.Sh PUBLISHING
The content directory is walked top-down.
.Bl -bullet
.It
Files whose names end in
.Pa .md
are pages.
The match is case-sensitive:
.Pa NOTES.MD
is copied as a file.
.It
Every other regular file is copied to the same path in dist.
Symbolic links to files are copied as files; symbolic links to directories are not
followed.
.It
Names starting with
.Sq \&.
are never published, at any depth, except directories named
.Pa .well-known .
Hidden files inside
.Pa .well-known
are still skipped.
This covers
.Pa .git ,
.Pa .github ,
.Pa .env
and the
.Pa .assetignore
files themselves.
.It
Never published: the dist and templates directories, the skeleton, and
.Pa site.toml
at the top level.
.It
A directory that contains a
.Pa .git
entry is skipped unless
.Ic nested_repos
is true.
.It
Paths matched by
.Pa .assetignore
or
.Ic ignore
are skipped, pages included.
.El
.Sh ASSETIGNORE
A
.Pa .assetignore
file may sit in any directory.
Its patterns follow
.Xr gitignore 5
exactly and are relative to that directory:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Blank lines and lines starting with
.Sq #
are ignored;
.Li \e#
starts a pattern with
.Sq # .
.It
.Sq \&!
re-includes what an earlier pattern excluded;
.Li \e!
is a literal
.Sq \&! .
A file cannot be re-included when a parent directory is excluded.
.It
A trailing
.Sq /
matches directories only.
.It
A
.Sq /
at the start or in the middle anchors the pattern to the file's directory; otherwise it
matches a name at any depth below it.
.It
.Sq *
and
.Sq \&?
do not match
.Sq / .
.Li [a-z] ,
.Li [!a-z] ,
.Li [^a-z]
and the ASCII classes
.Li [[:alpha:]] ,
.Li [[:digit:]] ,
etc. match one character.
.Li **/ ,
.Li /**
and
.Li /**/
cross directories.
.Sq \e
escapes the next character.
.It
Trailing spaces are removed unless escaped with
.Sq \e .
.It
Matching is case-sensitive.
A malformed pattern (an unterminated
.Sq \&[ ,
an unknown
.Li [:name:] ,
a trailing lone
.Sq \e )
never matches.
.El
.Pp
Later rules win.
.Ic ignore
patterns come first, then each directory's
.Pa .assetignore ,
parents before children.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# .assetignore for a site deployed with Cloudflare Workers
worker.js
wrangler.jsonc
builder/
.Ed
.Sh OUTPUT
.Bl -column "dir/foo/index.md" "dir/foo/index.{html,md,txt}" "/dir/foo/" -offset indent
.It Sy Source Ta Sy Output Ta Sy URL
.It Pa index.md Ta Pa index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /
.It Pa foo.md Ta Pa foo/index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /foo/
.It Pa dir/index.md Ta Pa dir/index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /dir/
.It Pa dir/foo.md Ta Pa dir/foo/index.{html,md,txt} Ta Pa /dir/foo/
.El
.Pp
When both
.Pa foo.md
and
.Pa foo/index.md
exist,
.Pa foo.md
is published as
.Pa foo.{html,md,txt}
with the URL
.Pa /foo .
Drafts that are not built do not count.
In URLs, bytes other than
.Li A-Za-z0-9-._~/
are percent-encoded.
.Pp
.Pa .html
is the skeleton with the rendered page in it.
.Pa .md
is the page after templates, includes and the table of contents are resolved, with the
frontmatter removed and leading blank lines dropped.
.Pa .txt
is plain text wrapped at
.Ic text_width .
.Pp
dist also gets
.Pa .ssg-dist ,
a marker that lets later builds empty it, and
.Pa sitemap.xml
when
.Ic base_url
is set.
If two sources write the same file (an asset
.Pa index.html
next to
.Pa index.md ,
say), the page wins and a warning is printed.
.Sh FRONTMATTER
A page or template may start with a block of keys:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
---
title: "Setting up"          # a comment
date: 2024-05-01
order: 2
color: #fff
quote: 'it''s'
empty:
---
.Ed
.Pp
The block starts when the first line is
.Li ---
(blanks around it allowed, after an optional UTF-8 BOM) and ends at the next
.Li ---
line; a missing end is an error.
Inside, each line is blank, a
.Li #
comment, or
.Li key: value .
Keys use
.Li A-Za-z0-9_.- .
Values are strings:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li \(dqdouble\(dq
Everything between the first and the last
.Sq \(dq ,
verbatim: no escapes, so
.Li \(dq$a \eneq b$\(dq
and
.Li \(dqC:\enew\(dq
survive.
A
.Li # comment
may follow the closing quote.
.It Li \(aqsingle\(aq
Literal;
.Li \(aq\(aq
is a quote.
A comment may follow.
.It bare
Trimmed.
A
.Sq #
preceded by a blank starts a comment, so
.Li #fff
is kept.
.Li key:
alone is the empty string.
.El
.Pp
A later key replaces an earlier one.
Line endings may be LF, CRLF or CR.
Values may contain template syntax; it is evaluated like the body.
.Pp
Without a
.Li ---
line, the leading lines of the form
.Li key: \(dqvalue\(dq
(double quotes, ending the line, no comments) are read as keys, up to the first blank or
other line.
This older form exists for compatibility.
.Sh TEMPLATE SYNTAX
Tags are written
.Li {{ ... }} ;
blanks and tabs inside the braces are allowed.
Key names use
.Li A-Za-z0-9_.- ;
.Li else
and
.Li end
are reserved.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li {{key}}
The key's value.
An undefined key stays as written, with inner blanks removed
.Pq Li {{ toc }} No becomes Li {{toc}} .
.It Li {{extend \(dqname\(dq}}
Place this file's body in template
.Ar name
as its
.Li {{content}} .
Only as the first thing in a page or template body (leading blank lines allowed), once;
its line ending goes with it.
Anywhere else it is left as written.
.It Li {{include \(dqname\(dq}}
Insert template
.Ar name
here.
.It Li {{if key}} ... {{else}} ... {{end}}
Keep the first part if
.Ar key
is true, the
.Li {{else}}
part (optional) otherwise.
.It Li {{if not key}}
The same, negated.
.It Li \e{{
A literal
.Li {{ .
.El
.Pp
Text that starts with
.Li {{
but is none of these
.Pq Li {{ foo bar }} , {{}} , {{a:1}}
is left as written.
Template syntax is evaluated everywhere in the page, code blocks and code spans included;
write
.Li \e{{
there to show braces.
.Pp
A template
.Ar name
is a path relative to the templates directory, with
.Pa .md
added unless it ends in
.Pa .md .
Absolute paths,
.Li ..
components and an empty
.Li {{include \(dq\(dq}}
are errors; an empty
.Li {{extend \(dq\(dq}}
is dropped silently and the page is built with no template.
.Pp
A key is true when it is defined and its value, trimmed, is not empty and not
.Li false ,
.Li 0 ,
.Li no
or
.Li off
in any case.
An
.Li {{if}} ,
.Li {{else}}
or
.Li {{end}}
alone on its line (blanks allowed) removes the whole line.
Branches not taken are not evaluated, so an include in one need not exist.
.Li {{if}}
nests up to 256 deep.
.Ss Evaluation
.Bl -enum
.It
The page's frontmatter keys are read and its body kept.
.It
For each
.Li {{extend}}
in the chain, the template's frontmatter keys are added where not already set, and the
template's body, with
.Li {{content}}
set to the body so far, becomes the new body.
.It
Built-in keys are added where not already set.
.It
Every key's value is evaluated, then the body: keys are filled, conditionals and includes
resolved.
Conditionals therefore see the merged keys: a template can test a page key and a page a
template key.
.El
.Pp
Priority is page, then inner template, then outer template, then built-in keys; a page can
override even
.Ic url .
A key that refers to itself through other keys stays as written at the point of the cycle.
Nesting of keys and includes is limited to 64 levels and a result to 64 MiB.
.Pp
An included template's frontmatter keys are defaults for that include only; the
including file's keys win.
One trailing newline is removed from it, so
.Li Hi {{include \(dqname\(dq}}!
stays on one line.
Includes may nest, but may not
.Li {{extend}}
and may not form a cycle.
.Sh BUILT-IN KEYS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic url
The page's URL:
.Li / ,
.Li /guide/ ,
.Li /guide/setup/ .
.It Ic path
Source path relative to the content directory:
.Li guide/setup.md .
.It Ic build_date
.Li YYYY-MM-DD ,
UTC, from
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
when it is set.
.It Ic word_count
Words in the page's plain text, template text included.
A word is a run of non-space bytes with at least one ASCII letter or digit or non-ASCII
byte.
.It Ic reading_time
Minutes at 200 words a minute, rounded up, at least 1.
.It Ic toc
Table of contents; see
.Sx TABLE OF CONTENTS .
Empty, and so false, when the page has no level 2 to 6 heading.
.It Ic children
The child pages as a markdown list, one
.Li - [Title](/url/)
line each, sorted; empty when there are none.
.It Ic parent_url , Ic parent_title
The parent page.
.It Ic prev_url , Ic prev_title , Ic next_url , Ic next_title
The previous and next sibling, in sorted order.
.El
.Pp
The parent and sibling keys are not defined when there is no such page, so they stay as
written; test them with
.Li {{if prev_url}} .
While the first pass runs, all navigation keys,
.Ic toc ,
.Ic word_count
and
.Ic reading_time
are empty.
.Ss Keys with a meaning
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic title
Fills the skeleton's
.Li <title> .
.It Ic nav_title , Ic page_title , Ic title
The first that is not blank is the page's title in
.Ic children ,
.Ic parent_title ,
.Ic prev_title
and
.Ic next_title .
Without any, the file name without
.Pa .md ,
or the directory name for an
.Pa index.md .
.It Ic order
A number; see
.Sx NAVIGATION .
.It Ic date
Sort key, compared as a string, so use
.Li YYYY-MM-DD .
Also the sitemap's
.Li <lastmod> .
.It Ic draft
When true, the page is built only with
.Fl \-drafts .
It may be set by a template.
.It Ic sitemap
When defined and false, the page is left out of
.Pa sitemap.xml .
.It Ic content
Set by
.Li {{extend}} ;
in the skeleton, the page's HTML.
.El
.Sh NAVIGATION
The parent of
.Pa dir/foo.md
is
.Pa dir/index.md ;
the parent of
.Pa dir/index.md
is the
.Pa index.md
one directory up.
Top-level pages have the root
.Pa index.md
as parent; it has none.
A page whose parent file does not exist has no parent and no siblings.
Siblings are the parent's children.
.Pp
Children are sorted by:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
.Ic order ,
ascending; pages with a numeric
.Ic order
come first.
It is read as a floating-point number; anything else, including
.Li nan ,
counts as no order.
.It
.Ic date ,
ascending as a string; dated pages come first.
.It
source path.
.El
.Sh TABLE OF CONTENTS
In a page or template,
.Li {{toc}}
becomes a markdown list of the page's level 2 to 6 headings, nested by level relative to
the shallowest, each linking to the heading's id.
It is put on lines of its own with blank lines around, so it should stand on a line of
its own (not inside a list or quote).
In the skeleton,
.Li {{toc}}
is the same list as HTML.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{{if toc}}
**Contents**

{{toc}}
{{end}}
.Ed
.Sh SKELETON
One HTML file wraps every page.
.Bl -bullet
.It
The page's HTML replaces whatever is inside the first
.Li <main ...>
\&...
.Li </main>
(case-insensitive), or goes where
.Li {{content}}
is if the skeleton has one.
Without either, the build fails.
.It
If the page has a
.Ic title
key, its value, HTML-escaped, replaces the text inside the first
.Li <title> ;
otherwise the skeleton's own text stays.
.It
.Li {{key}}
is any of the page's keys after evaluation, built-in keys included, HTML-escaped
.Pq Li & < > \(dq \(aq .
.Li {{content}}
and
.Li {{toc}}
are inserted as HTML.
.It
.Li {{if}} ,
.Li {{if not}} ,
.Li {{else}} ,
.Li {{end}}
and
.Li \e{{
work as in templates; unbalanced conditionals are an error.
.Li {{include}} ,
.Li {{extend}}
and undefined keys are left as written.
.El
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>My site</title>
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://example.com{{url}}">
</head>
<body>
{{if draft}}<p class="draft">Draft</p>{{end}}
<main>
</main>
<footer>Built {{build_date}}.</footer>
</body>
</html>
.Ed
.Sh MARKDOWN
CommonMark 0.31.2 (all 652 spec examples pass), plus, unless
.Ic extensions
is false:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
GFM tables (a delimiter row with
.Sq | ;
.Li \e|
in a cell is a literal pipe), task lists
.Li - [x] ,
strikethrough
.Li ~x~
and
.Li ~~x~~ ,
bare autolinks.
.It
footnotes
.Li [^label]
with
.Li [^label]: text ,
and inline
.Li ^[text] .
.It
definition lists: a term line, then
.Li ": definition" .
.It
alerts
.Li > [!NOTE] ,
.Li [!TIP] ,
.Li [!IMPORTANT] ,
.Li [!WARNING] ,
.Li [!CAUTION] .
.It
containers
.Li ::: name Optional title
\&...
.Li ::: ,
rendered as
.Li <div class="alert name"> .
.It
.Li ==mark== .
.It
heading attributes
.Li ## Title {#id .class} .
.El
.Pp
Raw HTML, heading ids and the sanitizer are set by the
.Ic [markdown]
table.
The
.Pa .txt
output renders the same tree as plain text: setext-style underlined headings, links as
.Li text <url> ,
lists and tables laid out, wide characters counted as two columns.
.Sh SITEMAP
With
.Ic base_url
set,
.Pa sitemap.xml
lists every built page, sorted by URL, as
.Li <loc>
holding
.Ic base_url
followed by the page URL, plus
.Li <lastmod>
when
.Ic date
starts with
.Li YYYY-MM-DD
(alone or followed by
.Sq T
or a blank).
Pages with a false
.Ic sitemap
key are left out.
A
.Pa sitemap.xml
in the content directory is copied instead, with a warning.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A series: a section index and two posts that share a layout.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
==> templates/base.md <==
# {{page_title}}

{{content}}

==> templates/post.md <==
---
page_title: "{{series}}: {{title}}"
---
{{extend "base"}}
{{content}}

{{if prev_url}}Previous: [{{prev_title}}]({{prev_url}}){{end}}
{{if next_url}}Next: [{{next_title}}]({{next_url}}){{end}}

{{include "partials/back"}}

==> templates/partials/back.md <==
Back to [{{parent_title}}]({{parent_url}}).

==> guide/index.md <==
---
title: "Guide"
---
{{children}}

==> guide/setup.md <==
---
title: "Setup"
series: "Guide"
order: 1
---
{{extend "post"}}
Install it.

==> guide/usage.md <==
---
title: "Usage"
series: "Guide"
order: 2
---
{{extend "post"}}
Use it.
.Ed
.Pp
.Pa dist/guide/setup/index.md
comes out as:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Guide: Setup

Install it.



Next: [Guide: Usage](/guide/usage/)

Back to [Guide](/guide/).
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Li {{if prev_url}} ... {{end}}
line is not a standalone tag, so when false it leaves an empty line; markdown ignores it.
.Pa /guide/
lists both posts as
.Li - [Guide: Setup](/guide/setup/)
and
.Li - [Guide: Usage](/guide/usage/) :
.Ic page_title
comes before
.Ic title
for link titles.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssg 1 ,
.Xr gitignore 5
.Pp
In the source tree:
.Pa docs/configuration.md ,
.Pa docs/templates.md ,
.Pa docs/markdown.md ,
.Pa docs/cli.md ,
.Pa docs/getting-started.md .
